=== I2S START/DROP stress: 100 cycles, TX starved every 5 ===

slab : free blocks per direction, read BEFORE each cycle. It must stay

       at 8. Falling means the driver is losing the DMA's in-flight

       block on every DROP; rising above 8 means a block was freed

       twice and the free list has a cycle in it.

starve: TX is left to run dry, which drives the driver down its

       tx_disable path -- the one place the leak fix could double-free.

  stress   1: slab tx=8 rx=8

  stress   2: slab tx=7 rx=7

  stress   3: slab tx=6 rx=6

  stress   4: slab tx=5 rx=5

  stress   5: slab tx=4 rx=4   TX starved on purpose

  stress   6: slab tx=4 rx=3

  stress   7: slab tx=3 rx=2

*** STRESS: SLAB EXHAUSTED at cycle 8: tx=2 rx=1 of 8.

    The driver leaks one block per direction per START/DROP.

    Starting anyway would block FOREVER inside i2s_buf_write(),

    which allocates with K_FOREVER -- no error, no log line.

    Fix: scripts/patch_zephyr_i2s_leak.sh ***

  final census: tx=2 rx=1 of 8

